  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_lace_cb46f8f84bc013da80bc41e4c26647fb020ef40031f3334686899c9a89cd3ea23a">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>lace, a string or cord serving to draw together opposite edges of clothing (bodices, stays, boots, shoes) by being passed through eyelet-holes or over hooks and pulled tight (OED s.v. lace n. 3); here measured in gross — so not lace n. 6 (the openwork fabric, measured in yards). Made of thread, leather, hair, worsted or caddis. For gold/silver decorative braid see passemain; see also point, scholas (shoelaces), aglett.</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
